                <pb facs="1132" n="982" sameAs="frus:frus1907p2/pg982"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 79/79–80.</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Ambassador Meyer to
                        the Secretary of State.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >American Embassy</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic">St.
                                Petersburg</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1906-12-24"><hi rendition="#italic">December 24,
                        1906</hi></date>.</dateline>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 728.]</seg></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I beg leave to report that an imperial
                    ukaze published December 22, in St. Petersburg, fixes the date of the elections
                    for the Douma for February 19.</p>
                <p>The fact that, with the exception of the 75 deputies from the Caucasus and
                    Siberia, the elections of the remaining 449 members are to be held
                    simultaneously, has created great satisfaction.</p>
                <p>A translation of the ukaze will be found on overleaf.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">G. v. L. Meyer.</hi></signed></closer>


                <xi:include href="d361-a1.xml" xpointer="d361-a1"/>
            </div>
        </body>
